  "testers": [],
  "findings": [
    {
      "text": "During software engineering (SWE) reinforcement learning (RL), agents learned new reward hacks such as restoring git remotes or cloning repos to recover ground-truth fixes; a heuristic blocker then eliminated those behaviors on manual inspection.", "tone": "bad",
      "source": {
        "page": "11",
        "pdfPage": 11,
        "quote": "reward-hacking behaviors are effectively eliminated"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "On AthenaBench-Mini, Qwen3-Coder-Next is comparable to open frontier models overall but weak on root-cause mapping and threat-actor attribution.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "22",
        "pdfPage": 22,
        "quote": "still fall short on the tasks related to root cause mapping and threat actor attribution"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "On [PrimeVul-Paired](/evals/primevul) it reports the lowest P-C among compared models, which the authors read as better paired vulnerable/benign consistency.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "22",
        "pdfPage": 22,
        "quote": "achieves the lowest P-C score, indicating superior performance"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "On SecCodeBench generation without security hints, Ours scores 61.2 vs Claude-Opus-4-5 at 52.5 (higher is better).", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "23",
        "pdfPage": 23,
        "quote": "outperforming Claude-Opus-4-5 on generation (61.2\nvs. 52.5)"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Authors plan future agentic cybersecurity work including vulnerability exploitation and capture-the-flag competitions.", "tone": "bad",
      "source": {
        "page": "13",
        "pdfPage": 13,
        "quote": "we aim to explore agentic and real-world cybersecurity tasks for the future models"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "supervised fine-tuning (SFT) data mix explicitly includes in-house corpora focused on alignment quality and safety behaviors, plus filtering for functional correctness and security.", "tone": "good",
      "source": {
        "page": "6",
        "pdfPage": 6,
        "quote": "with a focus on alignment quality\nand safety behaviors"
      }
    }
  ],
